    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_moccasin_represents_schedule_retenti",
          "text": "Moccasin represents the schedule with retention intervals. For each node in the graph, the method allows up to a small constant number of intervals, each specified by an integer start event and an integer end event, indicating when that node's output tensor is computed and how long it stays in memory.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "moccasin",
            "represents",
            "schedule",
            "retention",
            "intervals",
            "node",
            "graph",
            "method",
            "allows",
            "small"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_boolean_flag_marks_whether_interval",
          "text": "A Boolean flag marks whether each interval is actually active, so a node need not be recomputed a fixed number of times. The objective minimizes the total duration, a weighted sum over the active compute events where the weights are node execution times.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "boolean",
            "flag",
            "marks",
            "whether",
            "interval",
            "actually",
            "active",
            "node",
            "need",
            "not"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_memory_budget_enforced_through_const",
          "text": "The memory budget is enforced through the constraint programming cumulative constraint, treating tensor sizes as resource demands and the budget as capacity, while data dependencies between predecessors and successors are handled with the reservoir constraint.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "memory",
            "budget",
            "enforced",
            "through",
            "constraint",
            "programming",
            "cumulative",
            "constraint",
            "treating",
